A '''Mystery Man''' (Japanese: '''{{tt|謎の男|なぞのおとこ}}''' ''Mystery Man'' or '''なぞのせいねん''' ''Mystery Man'') is a type of [[Pokémon Trainer]] that debuted in {{game|Crystal}}, though it was originally translated as '''Mysticalman''' in the English version of Pokémon Crystal. Two important [[non-player character]]s have had this class, both of which are, as the name implies, mysterious men. In Crystal Version, [[Eusine]] had the title of "Mysticalman", but it was changed to the later translation of "Mystery Man" in {{game|HeartGold and SoulSilver|s}}. [[Ardos]] has this Trainer class in {{Pokémon XD}} during his cutscene battle with [[Zook]], before his affiliation with [[Cipher]] is known. For his battles with the {{player}}, however, his true class of {{tc|Cipher Admin}} is used.

Under this class, Ardos only reveals one member of his powerful team, his {{p|Alakazam}}. Eusine keeps a varied team, two thirds of which have some connection to mystical powers. He is searching for the [[Legendary Pokémon]] {{p|Suicune}}.

This Trainer class is also given to the character {{DL|Pokéstar Studios characters|River}}, as portrayed by {{tc|Fine Actor}} Terrence in parts two and three of [[The Giant Woman! Series]].

